// @vibe/compiler/entry/compiler — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-internal
// contract. This is entry/'s own top-level facade and the LAST directory in
// issue #897's explicit "high risk" grouping ("高リスク (要個別設計判断)
// ... entry/ とそのサブディレクトリ"), migrated last in this batch (after
// its two dependencies, entry/compiler/fs_compile/ and
// entry/source_compile/, both migrated earlier in the same batch, so this
// facade's `export` targets are already package boundaries by the time this
// contract is written).
//
// Pure re-export facade, ZERO real fn bodies of its own: compiler.vibe (the
// old index.vibe, renamed -- see naming note below) is three `export <path>
// { names }` cross-package SReExport blocks and nothing else -- forwarding
// a curated 20-name subset from ../source_compile (2 names),
// ./fs_compile (11 names), and ./file_compile (7 names). Same shape as
// codegen/index.vpkg's `export ./common_base { .. }` block, just with no
// locally-owned names alongside it (codegen.vibe additionally owns 8 real
// compile_* bodies; compiler.vibe owns none). check_contract's
// collect_impl_fn_defs finds nothing here (no SLet at all, since there are
// no real fn/let bodies), so nothing forces a "must declare" obligation --
// but every name below still needs a bodyless declaration anyway, because
// OTHER code that imports `../entry/compiler { name }` type-checks against
// THIS contract's declared signatures, not against the underlying packages
// directly (same reasoning as codegen/index.vpkg's re-exported-from-
// common_base names).
//
// Signature source of truth: source_compile.vibe's own real bodies (via
// entry/source_compile/index.vpkg), fs_compile.vibe's own real bodies (via
// entry/compiler/fs_compile/index.vpkg), file_compile.vibe's own real
// bodies (via entry/compiler/file_compile/index.vpkg, already migrated).
// Note fs_compile.vibe ALSO independently exports its own
// `compile_file_fs` / `compile_file_fs_module` / `prepare_file_fs_cached` /
// `compile_file_fs_cached` / `compile_file_fs_module_cached` (older,
// self-contained implementations) under the SAME names as file_compile.vibe's
// newer versions -- compiler.vibe deliberately does NOT re-export
// fs_compile's copies of these five names (only file_compile's, via the
// `export ./file_compile { .. }` block), so there is no ambiguity here:
// each declared name below traces to exactly one real body, matching
// compiler.vibe's own unchanged selection.
//
// Naming: no collision (entry/compiler/compiler.vibe did not exist), old
// index.vibe moved verbatim to compiler.vibe, same convention as
// loader.vibe/runtime.vibe/core.vibe/wasi_only.vibe/source_compile.vibe.
//
// External-caller fixes: the four
// `probe_lex_source_by_path` / `probe_parse_source_by_path` /
// `probe_source_control_by_path` / `probe_parse_stmt_progress_source_by_path`
// calls in selfbuild_gate_block_a.vibe that referenced the literal
// "lib/@vibe/compiler/entry/compiler/index.vibe" path (a manifest-derived
// `compiler_sources()` array key, not an import) are updated to
// ".../compiler.vibe" to track the manifest row rename below. No other
// literal `entry/compiler/index.vibe` leaf-path references exist repo-wide
// (confirmed via grep) -- every real caller already used the bare
// package-form `import ../entry/compiler { .. }` / `import ./entry/compiler
// { .. }`.
//
// No import cycle found: this directory's three export targets
// (../source_compile, ./fs_compile, ./file_compile) don't import back into
// entry/compiler/ (confirmed by reading all three; none references
// `entry/compiler` at all).
//
// Compiled into the compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv
// (group `entry`): the old single `entry/compiler/index.vibe` row becomes a
// dual row (this contract + compiler.vibe).
//
// No exported types: TypeDb (../../runtime, via fs_compile/file_compile)
// arrives as structural signature text (loader/runtime precedent -- no
// re-import needed here).

// --- re-exported from ../source_compile
fn compile_source(source: String) -> Bytes with Exception
fn compile_source_wasi(source: String, entry_name: String) -> Bytes with Exception

